    "rating": 0,
    "about": "Furnished flat share !\n    --------------------------------\n    All our flats are located in the city centre and close to all amenities\n    and public transport (Metro, Tramway and Bus).\n    ---------\n    This lovely private room in a fully equipped, furnished and turn-key flatshare in Toulouse grants comfort and design. It has household furnishings, including a double bed with pillows and duvet What is missing is your belongings to settle in your new home! The room has a lock if you want to close it.\n    All our rooms are fully furnished (bed, desk, wardrobe, duvet, pillows...).\n    ---------\n    The flatshare is located in the \"Capitole\" neighborhood, in the heart of Toulouse. A lot of restaurants, shops, public transports can be found close by. The apartment is on floor #1 . It is entirely furnished and is composed of a fully equipped kitchen with refrigerator, kitchen ustensils, toaster, kettle, crockery, microwave, pans… The accommodation also contains an iron, an ironing board, a clothes rack, a washing machine.\n You will also find cleaning items directly in the apartment: broom, dustpan and brush, bagless hoover, mop and bucket… Every furnished flatshare includes all bills: water, housing insurance, electricity, household waste tax, condominium fees, unlimited wi-fi.\n    All our flats are fully equipped (washing machine, dishes, decoration...)\n    by our teams, who also take care of the technical and material maintenance.\n    ---------\n    Want to know more about the Capitol neighbourhood? This lovely room in an all-inclusive flatshare is located in one of the liveliest neighbourhoods in Toulouse! The Capitol neighbourhood is the historical centre of the Pink’s city. It develops around the Capitol square, which has given it its name. Capitol Square is a place for the Toulousians to come together, share and enjoy their lives during major events. We find here the Capitol – an ancient and majestic building which is today the city hall of Toulouse. The Capitol Theatre abuts on this square as well. This historical building was inaugurated in the 19th century and it is devoted to ballet and lyric art. At the edge of the River Garonne, close to the Carmes neighbourhood, Capitol neighbourhood is simultaneously one of the smallest and richest neighbourhoods in Toulouse. Plenty of Museums and historical buildings are located here such as the Musée du Vieux Toulouse, the Musée des Augustins but also the Basilique Notre-Dame de la Daurade and the Basilique Saint-Sernin de Toulouse. The area is very well-connected by public transportations and counts an endless number of bars, restaurants and shops as well as prestigous universities such as the Toulouse Law School (University Toulouse 1 Capitol) \n    ---------\n    Minimum stay : 1 mois\n    Apartment eligible for CAF up to 258€ / month. The CAF for Caisse\n    d'allocations familiales is a free public service eligible for all,\n    including foreigners and can help you financially to pay part of your\n    housing according to your situation whether you are French or foreign. To\n    find out the potential amount of your assistance, go to the CAF website and\n    complete the online APL (housing assistance) estimate.\n    Service fee : from 690€\n    The service fee covers the writing of the lease but also the assistance\n    throughout your stay. The service fee covers the repair and maintenance of\n    the equipment as well as access to our ultra-reactive support in case of\n    need for intervention in your accommodation.\n    Deposit : 700€",
